  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe `report` job of `.github/workflows/post-merge.yml` has `needs: gate` and an `if` with no status check function. GitHub then adds an implicit `success()`. When the gate fails, the job is skipped before GitHub reads the expression. Thus a red `main` opened no rolling issue (run 43535610115, as #1611 says).\n\n- `.github/workflows/post-merge.yml`: the `if` of the `report` job now starts with `always() &&`. The other terms do not change:\n  - `needs.gate.result == 'success' || needs.gate.result == 'failure'`: a cancelled or a skipped gate still reports nothing.\n  - `needs.gate.outputs.skipped != 'true'`: a run that yields to a cut still reports nothing.\n  - The ref terms: a dispatch of a non-main ref still reports nothing.\n- A comment on the job says why `always()` is necessary.\n- No trigger, permission, runner label or step changes.\n\nThe red path after the gate already works: the gate job uploads `gate-output.txt` with `if: always()`, and `.github/scripts/post-merge-report.sh` reads `STATUS=failure` and the FAIL rows.\n\n## Tests\n\nPinned by `a_failed_gate_still_runs_the_report_job` (new file `xtask/tests/post_merge_report.rs`, in the same form as `xtask/tests/post_merge_concurrency.rs`). It reads the workflow and asserts:\n- the `if` of the `report` job starts with `${{ always() && `;\n- the `success` / `failure` term and the `skipped` term are still there.\n\nWithout the workflow change, the test fails with: `the report job's if starts with always(): ${{ (needs.gate.result == ...`.\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`, Linux): `xtask unit tests` ok (the new test ran and passed).\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The workflow YAML parses (`yaml.safe_load`), and the `if` value is as above.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real post-merge run. A red run on the self-hosted runner (`camcraft-post-merge`) is the full check: `report` runs and opens or comments on `main is red (post-merge gate)`, and the next green run closes it.\n- `actionlint` is not installed on this machine, and did not run.\n\n## Notes\n\n- A `.github/` change from a fork: read, not built. It waits for the maintainer (`needs-maintainer`).\n- `xtask/` is a process file (the new test). The PR does not edit `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`. A fork needs no action.\n- Branch base: `upstream/main` `e7f5f4315`. No context scout ran; this session did its own searches.\n\nProcess change: yes\nChangelog: none\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #1611\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
